    {
      "id": "part-1",
      "title": {
        "en": "Part 1"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_1005_uni4",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_1005_uni1",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Selena \"Extra Attacks\" Mark and Coordinated Attack"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Selena's gimmick is mainly about \"Extra Attacks\"\nSelena has two forms, Coordinated Attack and Mark, but Mark is the main one\nMark is a debuff inflicted upon enemies\nWhenever any Ally uses an attack card, the owner of a Mark, Extra Attacks\nEvery single target with a Mark owned by them one time ( Allies include self)\nMulti Hit Attack Cards still only trigger Mark once\nThe enemy takes Equivalent to a 0 cost 100% base Multiplier card\nMarks specifically damages Tenacity as well to help \"Ravage/Break\"\nRegular Extra Attacks like Coordinated Attack do not do damage Tenacity\nExtra Attacks can Crit\nTarget Spotted 1: Attunement random enemy is not an Extra Attack\nBut it is also not an attack card used, so it doesn't trigger Mark"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Selena \"Tenacity Damage\", \"Ravage\" and \"Recharge Tenacity\""
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Another of Selena's Mechanics is Tenacity Damage on Tactical Manuveur\nTenacity Damage means it deals 1 Full Bar of Tenacity regardless of Weakness\nTenacity is also decreased by Attack cards in different ammounts\nExamples:\n2 Cost Attack against Weakness = 2 Full Bars of Tenacity\n1 Cost Attack against Weakness = 1 Full Bar of Tenacity\n0 Cost Attack against Weakness = 1/2 Bar of Tenacity\nIf the enemy is not weak, characters do 1/3rd of the usual damage to Tenacity\nNon Targeted Attacks deal 1/2 of the usual damage to Tenacity\nWhen the enemy Tenacity bar is fully broken, they enter the Ravaged State\nRavaging an enemy grants the team +1 AP and delays enemy action count +1\nCharacters unless they specifically have an Anti Ravage effects\nDo not deal extra damage to enemies that are Ravaged\nTactical Manuveur 4 is capable of Recharging Tenacity of an enemy\nEnemies only Recharge Tenacity on turn Start\nBy using Tactical 4, you can Ravage 2 times per turn, or just chip away earlier"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_1005_uni1",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Selena \"Attunement\", Precision Aim and Eternal Hunger"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Selena also has Attunement on Target Spotted\nAttunement is activated whenever the Card is Drawn\n\"Move\" from Confiscate is Draw only if Eternal Hunger comes from Deck\nPrecision Aim is capable of Drawing an Attunement Card then placing it on top\nUsual Flow Chart of Effects:\nPrecision Aim\nDraw Target Spotted -> Attunment Triggers -> Draw Card/Damage Etc\nPrecision Aim then can put Target Spotted back on top\nTo be able to be Drawn again\nPrecision Aim isn't bad, but Eternal Hunger is stronger because its adds AP too"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
